# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD elbow-1 32014 black
ADD elbow-2 32014 black
ADD bar-1 32557 black
CONNECT elbow-1.hole1? -> bar-1.hole1? STIFF
CONNECT elbow-2.hole1? -> bar-1.hole4? STIFF
WHY Starts the build by capping both ends of the long perpendicular connector with angled elbows, making a twin-armed yoke for the output stubs.

STEP 2
ADD worm-1 4716 lightbluishgray
ADD axle-1 3705 reddishbrown
CONNECT axle-1.axle1 -> worm-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT axle-1.axle2 -> bar-1.hole2 TURNS
WHY Locks a worm gear onto the brown drive axle and passes the axle through the yoke's centre hole, starting the input shaft.

STEP 3
ADD axle-2 3705 lightbluishgray
ADD axle-3 3705 lightbluishgray
ADD axle-4 3705 lightbluishgray
ADD axle-5 3705 lightbluishgray
ADD plate-1 32316 black
ADD plate-2 32316 black
CONNECT axle-2.axle1 -> plate-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT axle-3.axle1 -> plate-1.hole5 TURNS
CONNECT axle-4.axle1 -> plate-2.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT axle-5.axle1 -> plate-2.hole5 TURNS
WHY Threads four frame axles through the end holes of two long plates, building the cage that will carry the differential's gears.

STEP 4
ADD cap-1 18654 lightbluishgray
ADD housing-1 6573 darkbluishgray
CONNECT cap-1.hole1 -> axle-1.axle3 TURNS
CONNECT housing-1.hole1 -> axle-1.axle2 TURNS
WHY Slides a round spacer onto the drive axle and mounts the differential gear housing on the same axle so it can spin freely around it.

STEP 5
ADD yoke-1 32184 black
ADD pin-1 43093 blue
CONNECT pin-1.axle1 -> yoke-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT pin-1.pin1 -> housing-1.hole2 STIFF
WHY Locks a friction axle-pin into the small connector's cross hole, then presses its pin end stiffly into the housing's second hole, hanging a stub arm off the differential.

STEP 6
ADD bush-1 3713 red
ADD bush-2 3713 red
ADD bush-3 3713 red
ADD bush-4 3713 red
ADD gear-1 94925 lightbluishgray
ADD gear-2 94925 lightbluishgray
ADD gear-3 94925 lightbluishgray
ADD gear-4 94925 lightbluishgray
CONNECT gear-1.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-1.axlehole1 -> axle-2.axle3 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-2.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-2.axlehole1 -> axle-3.axle3 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-3.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-3.axlehole1 -> axle-4.axle3 LOCKED
CONNECT gear-4.axlehole1 -> axle-5.axle2 LOCKED
CONNECT bush-4.axlehole1 -> axle-5.axle3 LOCKED
WHY Builds four identical gear units, a reinforced 16-tooth gear locked to each frame axle and stopped by a red bush, ready to ring the housing.

STEP 7
CONNECT bar-1.hole3 -> axle-4.axle4 TURNS
WHY Seen from this angle the gear cluster now sits square around the housing, so the yoke's last free hole is dropped onto a frame axle to brace it.

STEP 8
ADD worm-2 4716 lightbluishgray
CONNECT worm-2.axlehole1 -> axle-1.axle4 LOCKED
WHY Locks a second worm gear onto the far end of the drive axle, giving the input shaft a stop at both ends so it can't slide out.

STEP 9
ADD plate-3 32316 black
ADD plate-4 32316 black
CONNECT plate-3.hole1 -> axle-2.axle4 TURNS
CONNECT plate-4.hole1 -> axle-3.axle4 TURNS
WHY Adds a second pair of long plates across the tops of two frame axles, doubling the structure's rigidity around the gear cluster.

STEP 10
ADD bar-2 32557 black
CONNECT bar-2.hole1? -> plate-3.hole5? STIFF
WHY Plugs a second long connector into the free end of a side plate, stretching the frame out toward the output end.

STEP 11
ADD cap-2 18654 lightbluishgray
ADD cap-3 18654 lightbluishgray
ADD elbow-3 32014 black
CONNECT cap-2.hole1? -> bar-2.hole2? STIFF
CONNECT cap-3.hole1? -> bar-2.hole3? STIFF
CONNECT elbow-3.hole1? -> bar-2.hole4? STIFF
WHY Caps the new connector's remaining holes with two round spacers and an elbow, shaping the far end where the output axle will sit.

STEP 12
WHY Rotating the model confirms the elbow and yoke line up square with the housing before the closing plates go on.

STEP 13
ADD bar-3 32557 black
CONNECT bar-3.hole1? -> plate-4.hole5? STIFF
WHY Mirrors step 10 on the other side, plugging a third long connector into the remaining side plate's free end.

STEP 14
ADD plate3-1 6632 black
ADD plate3-2 6632 black
CONNECT plate3-1.hole1? -> bar-3.hole2? STIFF
CONNECT plate3-2.hole1? -> bar-3.hole3? STIFF
WHY Adds two thin cover plates across the new connector, closing in the frame on this side.

STEP 15
ADD cap-4 18654 lightbluishgray
ADD axle-6 4519 black
CONNECT axle-6.axle1 -> elbow-3.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT cap-4.hole1 -> axle-6.axle2 TURNS
WHY Locks the last axle through the elbow to form the output stub and caps it with the final round spacer, completing the differential.
